OL,4,CRecord 5,200 heat-linked deaths        
OL,5,Cestimated in England this year         
OL,6,GMore than 5,000 people suffered heat-  
OL,7,Gassociated deaths in England this      
OL,8,Gsummer, the UK Health Security Agency  
OL,9,G(UKHSA) has estimated - the highest    
OL,10,Gnumber since records began in 2016.    
OL,12,FThe UK experienced its hottest summer  
OL,13,Fon record in 2026, and the estimated   
OL,14,F5,258 heat-linked deaths were twice    
OL,15,Fthe previous high of 2,985 in 2022.    
OL,17,FThe most deadly period of the year for 
OL,18,Fheat-related deaths was between 21 and 
OL,19,F28 June, when there were an estimated  
OL,20,F2,401 heat-associated deaths.          
OL,21,FTemperatures peaked at 38C in that     
OL,22,Fperiod.                                
